  "localChanges": [
    "The selected-I/O patch changes only checksum readers/writers, legacy sum and help/version output, and checksum record parsing in the generated dependency source. No shared runtime source changes.",
    "Each local bin records the real initial standard-descriptor errors, enters the runtime launch cwd, and calls the upstream uucore::bin!(uu_<utility>) entry. The recorded errors are returned only when that descriptor is selected for I/O, before later file opens can reuse a missing descriptor number. The crate has its own Cargo workspace and lockfile.",
    "The local cwd adapter reads the launch cwd through Waffle's runtime_proc.cwd import before entering upstream, so relative file operands follow the request cwd even when PWD names another directory or is absent.",
    "The coreutils family build runs one locale-selected Cargo build per checksum utility through the shared patched-libc environment, release settings, verifier and family stager. Each guest embeds only its English utility catalog, the common uucore catalogs and, except for legacy sum, checksum_common. The locale selection binds the owned source receipt hash, and each locale proof retains the generated catalog source.",
    "The Waffle test loads each guest lazily through the real runtime process worker and compares frozen stdout/status/stderr-presence observations after native oracle identity verification.",
    "The package-local preparation helper exports the exact pinned Git revision, applies the owned patch, copies the I/O adapter and parser regressions, and seals every generated source file. Cargo patches are isolated to this checksum workspace. All upstream notices remain intact."
  ],
